2. CANDIDATES ON DISK AND THE COMPARISON
----------------------------------------
Only one TX-AGG fixture exists in the repository:
  experiments/ptr-engine/longrun/tasks-v7/TX-AGG.v1.json
    sha256 = 178042c254f7b732f57603985de35adf8e3722f80507219103c0f7b259e81b03
    size   = 79427 bytes   schema = consonance.longrun-fixture/2
    task_id = TX-AGG ; generation = gen-7 ; fixture_version = TX-AGG.v1
    N = 100 ; wall_tokens = 4312 ; fetch_budget_tokens = 1024
             => 178042c2... != 2b416d82... (DIFFERENT BYTES, same identifiers)

Full-workspace byte scan (os.walk over the repo, 56,431 files, skipping
.git/node_modules/__pycache__/.venv, files <= 8 MB): ZERO files hash to
2b416d82... . The digest occurs only inside text of the 20 run manifests and
inside this rows family — never as a document.

Serialization probe (exhaustive over the plausible space): parsing the on-disk
document and re-serializing with schema in {/1,/2} x indent in {None,1,2,3,4} x
sort_keys in {True,False} x ensure_ascii in {True,False} x trailing newline in
{"", "\n"} produces NO match for 2b416d82... . The file has no CRLF and no
trailing newline. So the pinned digest is not a formatting/canonicalization
variant of the current file — the CONTENT differs.

Content-level proof of the difference (semantic, not cosmetic): 26 of 26 rows
that embed a `checkpoint` object match the on-disk checkpoints by id, turn,
question and source, but DISAGREE on `expected` / `answer_form`; 0 of 26 agree.
Examples (row value -> on-disk value):
  cp.TX-AGG.g00.d2  20786    -> 156145
  cp.TX-AGG.g01.d2  60786    -> 210513
  cp.TX-AGG.g00.d6  10131    -> 51443
  cp.TX-AGG.g02.d2  100786   -> 269767
The on-disk fixture is therefore a RE-GENERATED TX-AGG (same ids, gen-7,
TX-AGG.v1) with different document bodies and different ground-truth answers,
not the document those rows measured.

